          "title": "var and Text Blocks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. var",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`var` = ==local type inference== from the initializer",
                "Type is **static**: still strongly typed, not dynamic",
                "`var list = new ArrayList<String>()` is ==ArrayList==, not `List`",
                "Want the interface? Declare `List<String>`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Allowed",
                "Fails"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "locals",
                  "fields"
                ],
                [
                  "for-loop variables",
                  "method parameters"
                ],
                [
                  "lambda parameters",
                  "return types"
                ],
                [
                  "`var x = 1;`",
                  "`var x;`, `var x = null;`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Text Blocks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Delimiter `\"\"\"`; ==line break== after the opening one is required",
                "Incidental indent stripped: least-indented line or closing `\"\"\"`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "String s = \"\"\"",
                "    Hi %s \\",
                "    there\\s",
                "    \"\"\".formatted(\"Ann\");"
              ],
              "note": "joined line, kept trailing space, filled placeholder"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Gotcha",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`\\` at line end",
                  "joins lines"
                ],
                [
                  "`\\s`",
                  "keeps trailing space"
                ],
                [
                  "literal `\"\"\"`",
                  "must be escaped"
                ],
                [
                  "`.formatted(args)`",
                  "fills `%s`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "`var` is not `Object` or dynamic: `var x = 1; x = \"a\";` fails to compile."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Records",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Records",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a record is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`record Point(int x, int y) {}` = immutable ==data carrier==",
                "Generated: private final fields, canonical constructor",
                "Accessors `x()` and `y()`: {red:no get prefix}",
                "Also `equals`, `hashCode`, `toString`",
                "==Compact constructor==: no parameter list, for validation or normalising"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "record Range(int lo, int hi) {",
                "    Range {",
                "        if (lo > hi)",
                "            throw new IllegalArgumentException();",
                "    }",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rules and comparison",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Implicitly ==final==; cannot extend a class",
                "No instance fields beyond the components",
                "Can implement interfaces; static members and extra methods are fine",
                "Immutability is **shallow**: a `List` component can still be mutated"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Record",
                "Lombok @Value",
                "Plain class"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Fields",
                  "final",
                  "final",
                  "your choice"
                ],
                [
                  "Extend a class",
                  "no",
                  "no (class is final)",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "Collections",
                  "still mutable",
                  "still mutable",
                  "still mutable"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Copy and fit",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "record Order(List<String> items) {",
                "    Order {",
                "        items = List.copyOf(items);",
                "    }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "reassign the parameter; the compiler assigns the field afterward"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No setters, no inheritance",
              "text": "Use records for ==DTOs==, **map keys** and pattern-matching data. Not for JPA entities: they need mutability and a no-arg constructor."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sealed Classes and Interfaces",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Sealed Classes and Interfaces",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. A Closed Set of Subtypes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`sealed` + `permits` lists the only allowed subtypes",
                "The compiler knows the ==closed set==",
                "Records are implicitly `final`: a natural fit as permitted subtypes"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "sealed interface Shape permits Circle, Square {}",
                "record Circle(double r) implements Shape {}",
                "record Square(double side) implements Shape {}"
              ],
              "note": "Shape can have no other implementors"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Modifiers and Placement",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Modifier",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`final`",
                  "no further extension"
                ],
                [
                  "`sealed`",
                  "continues the restriction"
                ],
                [
                  "`non-sealed`",
                  "reopens the hierarchy"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each permitted subclass declares ==exactly one== of these",
                "`permits` may be omitted: subclasses in the {green:same source file}",
                "Otherwise: same {blue:package}, or same {blue:module} if named"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Compare and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Kind",
                "Subclasses allowed"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`final`",
                  "**zero**"
                ],
                [
                  "`sealed`",
                  "a **known list**"
                ],
                [
                  "open",
                  "**anyone**"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Compile errors are the point",
              "text": "A permitted subclass with no `final`, `sealed` or `non-sealed` fails to compile. Adding a new permitted type breaks every ==non-exhaustive switch==: the intended safety net."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Switch Expressions and Pattern Matching",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
