    {
      "title": "Virtual Threads",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Virtual Threads",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What They Are",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Virtual thread== (final in Java 21): JVM-scheduled **lightweight** thread",
                "Runs on a small pool of ==carrier== platform threads",
                "Blocks on I/O → **unmounts**; carrier runs another thread",
                "So you can have ==millions== of them"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Mount",
                    "sub": "on carrier",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Blocks on I/O",
                    "sub": "unmount",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Carrier free",
                    "sub": "runs another",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "I/O done",
                    "sub": "remount",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Platform vs Virtual",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Platform",
                "Virtual"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Maps to",
                  "1:1 OS thread",
                  "JVM-scheduled"
                ],
                [
                  "Cost",
                  "~1 MB stack",
                  "cheap"
                ],
                [
                  "Per task",
                  "pooled",
                  "**one per task**"
                ],
                [
                  "Best for",
                  "CPU-bound",
                  "blocking I/O"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Thread.ofVirtual().start(runnable)`",
                "`Thread.startVirtualThread(r)`",
                "`newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()` in try-with-resources",
                "Executor `close()` ==waits for all tasks=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "try (var ex =",
                "  Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()) {",
                "  ex.submit(() -> fetch(url));",
                "}  // close() waits"
              ],
              "note": "one virtual thread per task"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pooling virtual threads",
                "`synchronized` around blocking calls ==pins== the carrier (Java 21)",
                "Heavy `ThreadLocal` data; long CPU loops"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Never pool: one per task. Limit concurrency with a ==Semaphore==, not pool size. Prefer `ReentrantLock` to avoid pinning."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Java 21 Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Java 21 Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. var and Records",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`var`: ==locals only==, type inferred at compile time",
                "Needs an initializer; never fields or parameters",
                "`record R(int a) {}`: immutable, accessor `a()`",
                "Compact constructor validates; record is ==final==",
                "Records can implement interfaces, not extend classes"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sealed Types",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "sealed interface Shape permits Circle, Square {}",
                "record Circle(double r) implements Shape {}",
                "record Square(double side) implements Shape {}"
              ],
              "note": "records are implicitly final"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Subclass must be {green:final}, {blue:sealed} or {orange:non-sealed}",
                "Closed set gives ==exhaustive switch==, no `default`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Switch Patterns",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "double area = switch (shape) {",
                "  case null -> 0;",
                "  case Circle c when c.r() > 10 -> -1;",
                "  case Circle(double r) -> 3 * r * r;",
                "  case Square(double side) -> side * side;",
                "};"
              ],
              "note": "arrows, no fall-through; `yield` returns from a block"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Guards",
              "text": "A guarded case needs an unguarded case of that type after it."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Text Blocks and Virtual Threads",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`\"\"\"` text block strips incidental indent",
                "`newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()`: one per task, ==never pooled==",
                "Avoid `synchronized` around blocking calls (pinning)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
